<title>GERMANY: Hamburg passenger traffic falls 2.7 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Hamburg passenger traffic falls 2.7 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Passenger traffic at Hamburg airport (HAM) fell 2.7 percent year-on-year to 543,693 travellers in February, the German airport association ADV said.</p>
<p>This followed a 1.7 percent decline in January, the ADV monthly traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The following tables show 1997 passenger details with percentage changes on the same period 12 months ago.</p>
<p>Feb 1997			Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>Total				547,693	    Down  2.7</p>
<p>Domestic			   270,250	    Up    0.4</p>
<p>Europe			     259,028	    Down  2.4</p>
<p>Overseas			    15,739	    Down 32.1</p>
<p>Transit				2,568	    Down 48.8</p>
<p>Jan-Feb 1997		 Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>Total			    1,070,686	    Down  2.2</p>
<p>Domestic			   519,976	    Down  0.3</p>
<p>Europe			     513,672	    Down  0.9</p>
<p>Overseas			    31,168	    Down 30.9</p>
<p>Transit				5,695	    Down 40.4</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
</text>
